WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.450
A headline from a made-up town: the
rate of increase of crime is falling.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.810
The reporter reading it pauses.

3
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.340
Is that good news, or not?

4
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.760
There are two things in that
sentence: the amount of crime,

5
00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.050
and the rate at which it is changing.

6
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.300
So if the rate of increase is
falling, is crime itself falling?

7
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.690
Or has it peaked?

8
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.060
In this mission, you'll set the graph of
a quantity against time beside the graph

9
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:27.830
of its rate of change.

10
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.810
You'll meet the second derivative:
the rate of change of the gradient.

11
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.950
And you'll sort curves
into convex and concave,

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.250
and hunt for points of inflection.

13
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: decide
whether crime is falling.
